<h1>NYSIIS</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
Convert a name to a phonetic coding of up to six characters.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Generalization</strong> (I am a kind of ...)<br>
<a href="phoneticCoding.html"><em>phonetic coding</em></a> <a href="algorithm.html"><em>algorithm</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="jaroWinkler.html"><em>Jaro-Winkler</em></a>, <a href="doubleMetaphone.html"><em>double metaphone</em></a>, <a href="soundex.html"><em>soundex</em></a>, <a href="Levenshtein.html"><em>Levenshtein distance</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
<a href="http://www.dropby.com/NYSIIS.html" target="_blank">(JavaScript)</a> (in page source).
<h2>More information</h2>
<p>
<strong>Robert L. Taft</strong>, <em>Name Search Techniques</em>, New York State Identification and Intelligence System, Special Report No. 1, Albany, New York, December 1970.
</p>

